  "accuracyFacts": [
    "Fetch fulfills with a Response for HTTP statuses such as 404 or 500; rejection indicates network, policy, abort, or request-processing failure rather than a non-2xx status by itself.",
    "The Fetch Standard RequestInit dictionary contains method, headers, body, referrer, referrerPolicy, mode, credentials, cache, redirect, integrity, keepalive, signal, duplex, priority, and window. Attribution Reporting, Topics, Private State Token, and targetAddressSpace are browser-specific extensions outside that dictionary.",
    "A Response type can be basic, cors, default, error, opaque, or opaqueredirect; filtered opaque and opaqueredirect responses hide status/body/headers and expose status 0.",
    "Request and Response bodies are one-shot streams; consuming, locking, or disturbing the stream affects later readers, and clone tees the stream with possible buffering. Null bodies are consumed as empty byte sequences by ordinary readers, while parsers can reject malformed or empty input.",
    "The ResponseType set includes basic, cors, default, error, opaque, and opaqueredirect. Script cannot set RequestInit.mode to navigate; doing so throws TypeError.",
    "RequestInit cache modes are default, no-store, reload, no-cache, force-cache, and only-if-cached; only-if-cached requires same-origin mode. Referrer policy accepts the standard Referrer-Policy values.",
    "Deferred Fetch allocates a default 640 KiB quota per top-level traversable/tab, with 128 KiB initially reserved for cross-origin minimal delegation, 8 KiB default reservations for eligible cross-origin nested contexts, 64 KiB normal delegated reservations, and a 64 KiB cap per reporting origin.",
    "fetchLater is Window-only, secure-context-only, requires an active document and HTTP(S) potentially trustworthy URL, rejects unknown-length/ReadableStream bodies, uses connect-src, and disables service-worker mode.",
    "fetchLater returns a synchronous FetchLaterResult whose activated flag indicates invocation, not server delivery or response success; its response is ignored."
  ],
